Two pointers Technique
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
▶️ Definition

Two pointers is an algorithmic technique where you use two separate indices (pointers) to traverse a data structure (usually an array or linked list) either:

-> from two ends toward the center, or
-> one pointer chasing another, or
-> both moving in the same direction but at different speeds
depending on the problem.

*** Efficient for sorted arrays, linked lists, sliding windows, palindromes, etc.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧭 Common Types of Two Pointer Techniques
1. Opposite Direction Pointers (Start & End)
   Used when processing an array from both ends.
2. Same Direction / Sliding Window
   Both pointers move forward; one expands the window, the other shrinks it.
3. Fast & Slow Pointers
   One pointer moves faster than the other.
